## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to combine multiple auth standards (OIDC, SAML) with a per-request binding mechanism, a realistic replay-protection pattern, and per-tenant isolation.

## Key Concepts
- OIDC ID tokens and SAML assertions as inputs
- Internal JWT with tenant, aud, scopes and fingerprint binding
- Replay protection via per-token fingerprint cache
- OpenAPI security schema for internal tokens
- SAML-to-claims adapter mapping SAML to standard claims

## Code Example
```javascript
// Issuance sketch (pseudo)
function issueInternalJwt(userClaims, fingerprint) {
  const payload = { ...userClaims, fingerprint, iat: now(), exp: nowPlus(300) }
  return signJwt(payload, gatewayPrivateKey)
}
```

```javascript
// Verification sketch (pseudo)
function verifyInternalJwt(token, fingerprint) {
  const payload = verifyJwt(token, gatewayPublicKey)
  return payload.fingerprint === fingerprint && payload.exp > now()
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rotate fingerprints or handle lost headers?
- How would you test replay protection and tenant isolation end-to-end?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design distributed workflow with real systems concepts: saga orchestration, event sourcing, outbox pattern, and idempotent handlers under failure. Focuses on practical correctness and maintainability at scale.

## Key Concepts
- Saga orchestration across multiple services
- Event sourcing and outbox integration
- Idempotent handlers using correlationId and event.id
- Compensating actions for partial failures

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo orchestrator sketch
function onEvent(evt) {
  const key = `${evt.correlationId}:${evt.id}`;
  if (dedupe(key)) return;
  markHandled(key);
  switch (evt.type) {
    case 'OrderPlaced':
      enqueue('ReserveInventory', { orderId: evt.orderId, items: evt.items }, evt.correlationId);
      break;
    case 'InventoryReserved':
      enqueue('AuthorizePayment', { orderId: evt.orderId, amount: evt.total }, evt.correlationId);
      break;
    case 'PaymentAuthorized':
      enqueue('ShipOrder', { orderId: evt.orderId }, evt.correlationId);
      break;
    case 'OrderFailed':
      enqueue('ReleaseInventory', { orderId: evt.orderId }, evt.correlationId);
      enqueue('RefundPayment', { orderId: evt.orderId }, evt.correlationId);
      break;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

